#!/usr/bin/with-contenv bash
# ArtisanHub: OrcaSlicer starts in its dark mode. Only a new /config gets this; an OrcaSlicer.conf that
# already exists is never changed, so a person's own choice in Preferences stays theirs.

CONF_DIR="/config/.config/OrcaSlicer"
CONF="${CONF_DIR}/OrcaSlicer.conf"

if [[ ! -e "${CONF}" ]]; then
  mkdir -p "${CONF_DIR}"
  printf '{\n\t"app": {\n\t\t"dark_color_mode": "1"\n\t}\n}\n' > "${CONF}"
  chown abc:abc /config/.config "${CONF_DIR}" "${CONF}"
  echo "[ahi-init] OrcaSlicer set to start in dark mode"
fi

# B49: files the farm sends to this desktop open in the OrcaSlicer already running (svc-ahi-inbox). OrcaSlicer
# hands a file to its running window only with "single instance" on and a session bus to find it by, so both are
# set on every start: the setting in OrcaSlicer.conf, and the bus (svc-ahi-bus) in labwc's environment, which
# OrcaSlicer is started from. Without them a sent file would open a second OrcaSlicer.
if grep -q '"single_instance": false' "${CONF}" 2>/dev/null; then
  sed -i 's/"single_instance": false/"single_instance": true/' "${CONF}"
  echo "[ahi-init] OrcaSlicer set to a single instance"
elif ! grep -q '"single_instance"' "${CONF}" 2>/dev/null; then
  sed -i '0,/"app": {/s//"app": {\n\t\t"single_instance": true,/' "${CONF}"
fi

BUS_LINE="DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/config/.XDG}/ahi-bus"
LABWC_ENV="/config/.config/labwc/environment"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "${LABWC_ENV}")"
touch "${LABWC_ENV}"
grep -v '^DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=' "${LABWC_ENV}" > "${LABWC_ENV}.ahi" || true
printf '%s\n' "${BUS_LINE}" >> "${LABWC_ENV}.ahi"
grep -q '^NO_AT_BRIDGE=' "${LABWC_ENV}.ahi" || printf 'NO_AT_BRIDGE=1\n' >> "${LABWC_ENV}.ahi"
mv "${LABWC_ENV}.ahi" "${LABWC_ENV}"
chown -R abc:abc /config/.config/labwc
